  "about": "Each current capture of public/screens: \"captured\" the day it was added, \"verified\" the App Store version of the app it was last checked against (null: never checked; the nine captures of 24 Sept 2026 wait for one simulator session against the current build). The covers' detail and phone compositions refuse a capture whose \"verified\" is older than the store's version (ci/categories.json store.known, tools/ci/release.mjs): COVER_STALE_SCREEN. \"says\" (optional): the texts that read on the capture, copied from it by eye, so COVER_FACT can match a cover's word to the screen a film shows (tools/ci/cover.mjs). After checking a capture against the build the store has, set its \"verified\" to that version; after replacing it, its \"captured\" too. \"stale\" (2026-11-02, after TNET's notice): the capture still shows the car's price, the market, the wallet or the portfolio, which the app no longer has; the ones listed in ci/categories.json \"marketGone\".screens never reach a film until retaken (then drop \"stale\", update \"captured\" and \"verified\", and take the name out of that list). 04-wallet (the wallet itself) moved to public/screens/_retired.",
